# Emmer Static Site Generator - AI Assistant Guidelines

## Project Overview
Emmer is a static site generator built with Elixir/Phoenix that uses:
- **Solid templating** (Elixir implementation of Liquid templating language)
- **YAML configuration** for site data and page metadata
- **Tailwind CSS + DaisyUI** for styling and components
- **Live preview system** with real-time file watching
- **Phoenix LiveView** for the admin interface

## Directory Structure
```
my-site/
├── content/            # Source content (HTML + YAML)
│   ├── site.yaml       # Site-wide configuration
│   ├── index.html      # Home page
│   ├── index.yaml      # Home page data
│   ├── about.html      # About page
│   ├── about.yaml      # About page data
│   ├── blog.html       # Blog page
│   ├── blog.yaml       # Blog page data
│   ├── images/         # Static images
│   ├── css/            # Custom CSS files
│   └── js/             # Custom JavaScript files
├── templates/          # Solid/Liquid templates
│   ├── layout.html     # Main layout template
│   ├── header.html     # Header partial
│   ├── footer.html     # Footer partial
│   └── components/     # Reusable components
└── dist/               # Built output (auto-generated)
```

## Key Technologies & Conventions

### 1. Solid Templating (Liquid Implementation)
- **Variables**: `{{ variable_name }}`
- **Layouts**: `{% layout "layout.html" %}` (file extension optional - system adds .html automatically)
- **Includes**: `{% render "header.html" %}` (file extension always expected)
- **Includes with parameters**: `{% render "footer.html", tagline: site.tagline, name: site.name %}`
- **Conditionals**: `{% if condition %}...{% endif %}`
- **Loops**: `{% for item in items %}...{% endfor %}`

### 2. YAML Configuration
- **Site-wide data**: `content/site.yaml`
- **Page-specific data**: `content/page.yaml` (pairs with `page.html`)
- **Front matter**: YAML at top of HTML files between `---` markers
- **Data merging**: Site data → Page YAML → Front matter (front matter wins)

### 3. Tailwind CSS + DaisyUI
- **Utility-first CSS** with Tailwind classes
- **Component library** with DaisyUI components (btn, card, navbar, etc.)
- **Theme system** with light/dark mode support
- **Custom variants** for LiveView states

### 4. File Structure Conventions
- **Content files**: `.html` files in content directory
- **Data files**: `.yaml` files with same basename as HTML files
- **Templates**: `.html` files in templates directory
- **Assets**: Any non-HTML/YAML files in content directory

## Development Guidelines

### When Working with Templates
1. **Use Solid syntax** for all templating (not EEx)
2. **Layout system**: Use `{% layout "template.html" %}` for page structure
3. **Content placeholder**: Use `{{ content }}` in layout templates
4. **Template includes**: Use `{% render "partial.html" %}` for reusable components
5. **Variable access**: Use dot notation (e.g., `{{ site.name }}`, `{{ page.title }}`)

## Layout System Implementation

### How to Set Up a Layout Template
1. **Create layout file**: `templates/layout.html`
2. **Add content placeholder**: Use `{{ content }}` where page content should appear
3. **Add template includes**: Use `{% render "header.html" %}` and `{% render "footer.html" %}` for reusable parts (file extension required)
4. **Pass parameters**: Use `{% render "footer.html", tagline: site.tagline, name: site.name %}` to pass data to partials
5. **Access variables**: Use `{{ site.name }}`, `{{ page.title }}`, etc.

### How to Use a Layout in HTML Pages
1. **Add layout directive**: Place `{% layout "layout" %}` or `{% layout "layout.html" %}` at the top of your HTML file (file extension is optional)
2. **Add page content**: Write your HTML content after the layout directive
3. **Optional front matter**: Add YAML between `---` markers at the very top for page-specific data

### When Working with YAML
1. **Site data**: Define global variables in `site.yaml`
2. **Page data**: Create `.yaml` files alongside `.html` files
3. **Front matter**: Use `---` delimiters for inline YAML in HTML files
4. **Data hierarchy**: Site → Page YAML → Front matter (latter overrides former)
5. **Multi-line content**: Use YAML block scalars (`|`, `>`, `|-`) for long content

### When Working with Styling
1. **Use DaisyUI components** when possible (btn, card, navbar, etc.)
2. **Tailwind utilities** for custom styling
3. **Responsive design** with Tailwind breakpoint prefixes
4. **Theme support** with `data-theme` attributes
5. **LiveView states** with custom variants (phx-click-loading, etc.)

### When Working with Elixir Code
1. **Phoenix LiveView** for interactive components
2. **File watching** with `Emmer.FileWatcher`
3. **Build system** with `Emmer.Builder`
4. **Database** with Ecto for project management
5. **PubSub** for real-time updates

## Common Patterns

## Layout System Examples

### Complete Layout Template (`templates/layout.html`)
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>{% if page.title %}{{ page.title }} - {% endif %}{{ site.name }}</title>
    <meta name="description" content="{{ page.description | default: site.description }}">
</head>
<body>
    {% render "header.html" %}
    <main>
        {{ content }}
    </main>
    {% render "footer.html" %}
</body>
</html>
```

### Header Partial (`templates/header.html`)
```html
<header class="navbar bg-base-200">
    <div class="flex-1">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost text-xl" href="/">{{ site.name }}</a>
    </div>
    <div class="flex-none">
        <ul class="menu menu-horizontal px-1">
            <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
            <li><a href="/about">About</a></li>
            <li><a href="/blog">Blog</a></li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</header>
```

### Footer Partial with Parameters (`templates/footer.html`)
```html
<footer class="footer footer-center p-10 bg-base-200 text-base-content">
    <div class="grid grid-flow-col gap-4 md:place-self-center md:justify-self-end">
        <div class="text-center">
            <p class="text-lg font-bold">{{ name }}</p>
            <p class="text-sm">{{ tagline }}</p>
            <div class="mt-2">
                <p>{{ address_line_1 }}</p>
                <p>{{ address_line_2 }}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-4">
                <a href="mailto:{{ contact_mail }}" class="link link-hover">{{ contact_mail }}</a>
                <br>
                <a href="tel:{{ contact_number }}" class="link link-hover">{{ contact_number }}</a>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-2">
                <a href="{{ gmaps_url }}" target="_blank" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline">View on Map</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</footer>
```

### Using Footer with Parameters
```html
{% render "footer.html",
   tagline: site.tagline,
   name: site.name,
   address_line_1: site.address_line_1,
   address_line_2: site.address_line_2,
   gmaps_url: site.gmaps_url,
   contact_mail: site.contact_mail,
   contact_number: site.contact_number %}
```

### Page Using Layout (`content/about.html`)
```html
---
title: "About Us"
description: "Learn more about our company"
---
{% layout "layout" %}
<div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-6">{{ page.title }}</h1>
    <p class="text-lg mb-4">{{ page.description }}</p>
    <div class="prose">
        <p>This is the about page content that will appear in the main area.</p>
    </div>
</div>
```

### Site Configuration
```yaml
site:
  name: "My Site"
  description: "Site description"
  contact:
    email: "contact@example.com"
```

### Page Data
```yaml
page:
  title: "Page Title"
  description: "Page description"
  posts:
    - title: "Post 1"
      content: "Post content"
```

## AI Assistant Instructions

### When Helping with Templates
- Always use Solid/Liquid syntax, not EEx
- **Layout system**: Guide users to use `{% layout "template" %}` or `{% layout "template.html" %}` for page structure (file extension optional)
- **Template includes**: Show how to use `{% render "partial.html" %}` for reusable components (file extension always required)
- **Template parameters**: Demonstrate passing data with `{% render "partial.html", key: value, key2: value2 %}`
- **Content placeholder**: Explain that `{{ content }}` is where page content appears in layouts
- Suggest DaisyUI components for UI elements
- Use Tailwind utilities for custom styling
- Consider responsive design with breakpoints
- Include proper data variable references

### When Helping with YAML
- Follow the data hierarchy (site → page → front matter)
- Use appropriate YAML block scalars for content
- Ensure proper indentation and syntax
- Consider data organization and reusability

### When Helping with Styling
- Prefer DaisyUI components over custom CSS
- Use Tailwind utilities for layout and spacing
- Consider theme support (light/dark mode)
- Include responsive design considerations
- Use semantic class names

### When Debugging
- Check file paths and directory structure
- Verify YAML syntax and data structure
- Ensure template syntax is correct
- Check build logs for errors
- Verify asset paths and references

## File Extensions & MIME Types
- **HTML files**: `.html` (processed with Solid templating)
- **YAML files**: `.yaml` (data configuration)
- **CSS files**: `.css` (Tailwind + DaisyUI)
- **JavaScript files**: `.js` (Phoenix LiveView)
- **Image files**: `.png`, `.jpg`, `.svg`, etc. (static assets)

## Build Process
1. **File watching** detects changes in content, templates, or assets
2. **YAML parsing** loads site and page data
3. **Template processing** applies Solid templating
4. **Asset copying** moves static files to output directory
5. **Live preview** updates in real-time via Phoenix LiveView

## Common Issues & Solutions
- **Template not found**: Check templates directory and file names
- **Layout not working**: Ensure `{% layout "layout.html" %}` is at the top of your HTML file
- **Content not appearing**: Verify `{{ content }}` placeholder exists in your layout template
- **Template includes failing**: Check that partial files exist in templates directory
- **Template parameters not working**: Verify parameter names match between render call and partial template
- **Variable not defined**: Verify YAML data structure and variable names
- **Build errors**: Check YAML syntax and file paths
- **Styling issues**: Ensure Tailwind/DaisyUI classes are correct
- **Live preview not updating**: Check file watcher is running and try to rebuild manually. check if the file in the dist folder is reflecting the expected changes.

Remember: Emmer combines the simplicity of static sites with the power of modern web development tools, providing a fast, secure, and maintainable way to build websites.
